# SciGradify Biology → official England requirements (data/curriculum/requirements/england-biology.json).
# One line per requirement (its id without the "eng-" prefix):
#   <requirement> = <lesson> <F|P|I> <h|m|l> [; <lesson> <F|P|I> <h|m|l> …] [| what is missing, or why there is no match]
#   <requirement> = none | why no lesson teaches it
# F full: the lesson teaches everything the requirement asks, at least to the depth asked.
# P partial: the lesson teaches part of it; the note says what is missing across all lessons listed.
# I indirect: the lesson touches the requirement in passing, or teaches it only as a prerequisite or application.
# Confidence h/m/l is the mapper's, not a reviewer's. Every line was judged from the lesson's objectives and
# headings and, where those were ambiguous, a search of the lesson notes (scripts/curriculum/README.md).
# Status of the whole file: AI-drafted, unreviewed. Not verified by a teacher or examiner.
# A note starting "above:" means the content is covered but taught at a level well above the stage.

## Batch 1: national curriculum, key stages 1–3 (Biology)
nc-y1-plants-01 = none | No lesson teaches identifying common wild and garden plants or deciduous and evergreen trees by name; u11-05 mentions deciduous forest only as a biome.
nc-y1-plants-02 = u08-27 P m; u08-03 I m; u08-04 I m; u08-05 I m | above: flower, root, stem and leaf structure are taught at secondary depth; the basic whole-plant structure of common flowering plants and trees for young children is not taught directly.
nc-y1-animals-including-humans-01 = none | No lesson teaches identifying and naming common fish, amphibians, reptiles, birds and mammals.
nc-y1-animals-including-humans-02 = u11-04 P m; u11-06 I m | Herbivore, carnivore and omnivore appear as consumer roles in ecosystems; no lesson asks learners to identify and name common animals in each group.
nc-y1-animals-including-humans-03 = u01-07 I l | The animal kingdom's features are described; comparing the structure of fish, amphibians, reptiles, birds and mammals is not taught.
nc-y1-animals-including-humans-04 = u07-01 I l | Organ systems are outlined at secondary level; the senses and the body parts associated with each are not taught.
nc-y2-living-things-and-their-habitats-01 = u01-02 F m; u01-04 P m | above: taught as the characteristics of life and hard cases; "dead" versus "never alive" is covered by applying the characteristics.
nc-y2-living-things-and-their-habitats-02 = u11-03 P m; u11-04 P m; u06-04 I m | Habitat and niche, adaptation and interdependence are taught at secondary depth; meeting the basic needs of animals and plants in named habitats is not taught for this age.
nc-y2-living-things-and-their-habitats-03 = none | No lesson asks learners to identify and name plants and animals in habitats or microhabitats.
nc-y2-living-things-and-their-habitats-04 = u11-06 F h; u11-04 P m | above: food chains are taught fully; naming different sources of food for animals is not taught.
nc-y2-plants-01 = u08-31 P m; u08-32 I m | Germination and asexual reproduction (bulbs) are taught; observing seeds and bulbs growing into mature plants is not a lesson activity.
nc-y2-plants-02 = u08-31 P m; u08-12 I m | Water and temperature for germination, and light for photosynthesis, are taught; what plants need to grow and stay healthy is not drawn together.
nc-y2-animals-including-humans-01 = u07-32 I m | Human growth and development after birth are described; animals having offspring that grow into adults is not taught as a general idea for this age.
nc-y2-animals-including-humans-02 = u01-02 I m | Nutrition and respiration as characteristics of life imply the needs; the basic needs of animals (water, food and air) are not taught directly.
nc-y2-animals-including-humans-03 = none | No lesson teaches the importance of exercise, a balanced diet and hygiene for health.
nc-y3-plants-01 = u08-03 F h; u08-04 F h; u08-05 F h; u08-27 F h | above: roots, stems, leaves and flowers are each a lesson at secondary depth.
nc-y3-plants-02 = u08-11 P m; u08-31 I m; u08-12 I m | Mineral nutrients and the conditions for germination and photosynthesis are taught; room to grow and variation between plants is not.
nc-y3-plants-03 = u08-09 F h; u08-07 F h; u08-10 P h | above: water transport, xylem and transpiration (with a potometer) are taught.
nc-y3-plants-04 = u08-28 F h; u08-30 F h; u08-29 P h | above: pollination, seed formation and dispersal are taught.
nc-y3-animals-including-humans-01 = u07-22 P m; u11-04 P m | Digestion of food and the consumer role are taught; the right types and amounts of nutrition (a balanced diet) are not.
nc-y3-animals-including-humans-02 = u07-27 F h | above: functions of the skeleton and antagonistic muscles.
nc-y4-living-things-and-their-habitats-01 = u01-05 F m; u01-07 P m | above: taught as taxonomy and the kingdoms.
nc-y4-living-things-and-their-habitats-02 = none | No lesson teaches using or constructing classification (dichotomous) keys.
nc-y4-living-things-and-their-habitats-03 = u11-26 P m; u11-24 P m; u11-27 P m | above: climate change, habitat fragmentation and pollution as threats are taught at secondary depth.
nc-y4-animals-including-humans-01 = u07-21 F h; u07-22 F m | above: organs of the digestive system and their roles.
nc-y4-animals-including-humans-02 = none | No lesson teaches the types of human teeth and their functions.
nc-y4-animals-including-humans-03 = u11-06 F h; u11-07 F h; u11-17 P m | Food chains and webs are taught fully; predator and prey in u11-17.
nc-y5-living-things-and-their-habitats-01 = none | No lesson compares the life cycles of a mammal, an amphibian, an insect and a bird; u11-19 covers parasite life cycles only.
